cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hopforge in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "hopforge: a universal tight-binding engine for bands, topology, transport and response"
abstract: >-
  A universal tight-binding engine from 1D chains to 3D crystals and Wannier90 models: any
  lattice, orbitals, spin, spin-orbit coupling, magnetism, Slater-Koster bonding and
  discretised k.p models, with more than 40 published models. It computes bands, DOS, ribbons,
  slabs and flakes; Berry phases, Chern numbers, Wilson loops, Z2 and winding numbers;
  anomalous, spin and orbital Hall conductivities, Edelstein effects, Berry curvature dipole
  and orbital magnetisation; Kwant-style quantum transport; KPM and Kubo-Bastin for large
  systems; surface spectra; mean-field Hubbard, Floquet engineering and exact diagonalisation;
  and moire and orbitronics tools. It is benchmarked against published results and ships with
  tutorial notebooks and quizzes.
type: software
